  "student_passage": "Last Saturday, Nora took a box of toy cars to the school fair. The cars had belonged to her brother, (1) ____ he no longer played with them. Nora wanted to give them to younger children. Before the fair, she put a small price card on the box: “Free.”\n\nAt first, nobody took a car. “Perhaps they cannot see your card,” her friend said. Nora moved the card to the front. A little boy stopped and (2) ____ at a blue car. “How much is it?” he asked. Nora showed him the sign and explained that he could take it without (3) ____.\n\nThe boy smiled, but he did not leave at once. He wanted to (4) ____ something useful in return. He noticed that the box was nearly empty and offered to carry it to Nora's classroom later. Nora thanked him for his (5) ____ offer.\n\nBy noon, all the cars had new owners. Nora and the boy carried the box (6) ____ because it was light. They put it on a shelf for another fair. Nora had expected to lose a few old toys that day. Instead, she had (7) ____ a new friend. She decided to keep the same clear sign for the (8) ____ fair.",
